' ---------- notes ----------

note bottom of Document
  **Aggregate-root facade**: text / html / pages /
  outline() / hit() / confidence() / date /
  timeline() delegate to current_content.
end note

note right of DocumentContent
  **html is THE artifact**: sanitized semantic
  HTML; structural tags carry data-nid,
  data-pages, and data-date (EDTF) when dated
  — derived values burned into an immutable
  artifact cannot drift.
  text = plain projection + FTS index.
  --
  Lifecycle: new extractor ⇒ new snapshot ⇒
  fresh rows, immutable after commit;
  is_current + partial unique = DB-enforced
  "current"; pointer + flag flip in one
  transaction. Re-DATING = rebuild the
  snapshot from raw_output — no OCR cost,
  no second lifecycle.
  --
  **Ops, not schema**: prune old non-current
  snapshots, GC unreferenced blobs.
end note

note right of Node
  **SQL index into the one true HTML** —
  one row per data-nid tag.
  **The type IS the html tag**;
  the sanitizer allowlist is the vocabulary.
  level = semantic level; depth derivable
  from path. subtree = path LIKE 'prefix%';
  html()/text() are string slices.
end note

note bottom of PageRegion
  **Two-tier geometry**: polygon = truth
  (normalized closed ring, handles rotation);
  envelope derived for indexed SQL; hit() =
  envelope filter → point-in-polygon refine →
  smallest area. words: [[x0,y0,x1,y1,
  text_start,text_end,conf], …].
end note

note as DATE #EDF3EC
  **Information-origin dating** — when the
  content was RECORDED, not dates it mentions
  (a 1943 diary entry about 1918 ⇒ 1943;
  mentioned dates are evidence, not answers).
  Same house pattern as polygon/envelope:
  date_edtf (EDTF: "1943-05~", "194X",
  "1943-05-12/1943-05-20", "../1943-05") is
  lossless truth; date_min/date_max are
  derived strict bounds for btree overlap
  queries; NULL bound = open side —
  objects.overlapping(period) hides the null
  logic. date_source: EXPLICIT (printed),
  METADATA, INFERRED (model), INTERPOLATED
  (diary move: undated page between anchors
  gets [prev_anchor, next_anchor] — honest
  range, no fake midpoint), INHERITED
  (top-down), AGGREGATED (bottom-up envelope),
  CURATED. date_conf = belief in the
  attribution — scalar, NEVER mixed into the
  additive conf_stats.
  Rollup invariant: every dated child's range
  ⊆ parent's; AGGREGATED parents are tight
  envelopes of dated children.
end note

DATE .. Dated

note as STD #EDF3EC
  **Boring by construction**: content.html ≈
  hOCR; Node ≈ Tagged-PDF structure tree /
  docling items; PageRegion ≈ PAGE-XML region /
  docling prov; dates ≈ EDTF (ISO 8601-2,
